  "worked_solution": "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-\u22ef \\\\  & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{120}-\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get an expansion for ${x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x,$ we multiply this series by ${x}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & ={x}^{2}(x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{120}-\u22ef) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{7}}{120}-\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
